'''''Kindbergia praelonga''''', known as '''common feather-moss''', is a species of [[moss]] belonging to the family [[Brachytheciaceae]]. It is a medium to large size moss with [[pinnate]] branches.<ref name="ef">{{cite web |title=Kindbergia praelonga in Flora of North America @ efloras.org |url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=250099202 |website=www.efloras.org}}</ref> The species is of interest for having properties that may be beneficial for human health.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Evans |first1=Paul |title=Country diary: the quiet miracle of the common feather-moss |url=https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2020/jan/23/country-diary-the-quiet-miracle-of-the-common-feather-moss-wenlock-edge |website=the Guardian |access-date=22 November 2021 |language=en |date=23 January 2020}}</ref>

The species is found worldwide in moist to wet habitats.<ref name="ef"/> It is one of the most common mosses in lowland [[Great Britain]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Kindbergia praelonga |url=https://www.britishbryologicalsociety.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Kindbergia-praelonga.pdf |website=British Biological Society |access-date=23 November 2021}}</ref>

